      "problem": "Solve the equation $2| 2a - 4 | - 7 = 13.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we isolate the absolute value on the left side of the equation:\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2|2a-4|-7 & =13 \\\\ 2|2a-4| & =20 \\\\ |2a-4| & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following two cases:\n\n- If $|2a-4| = 2a-4,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|2a-4| & =10 \\\\ 2a-4 & =10 \\\\ 2a & =14 \\\\ a & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|2a-4| = -(2a-4),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|2a-4| & =10 \\\\ -(2a-4) & =10 \\\\ -2a+4 & =10 \\\\ -2a & =6 \\\\ a & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $a=-3$ and $a=7.$",
